---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import CodeBlock from '../components/CodeBlock.astro';
import { links, REPO } from '../data/site';

const protects = [
  ['A prompt-injected agent reading your secrets', 'Credential files such as ~/.ssh, cloud credentials and the HQ config are refused for every tool, always. Shell commands start with an empty environment plus a short allowlist, and the OS sandbox masks config, env files and private SSH keys.'],
  ['Data leaving after untrusted content', 'Once a session reads a web page, mail, a converted document, another agent\'s mailbox, a pane or a remote MCP result, project secrets and outbound network from bash are denied. Sub-agents share the taint, so delegating does not clear it.'],
  ['Server-side request forgery', 'web_fetch refuses loopback, private, link-local and metadata addresses, checks every redirect hop and pins the resolved address so DNS rebinding cannot move it.'],
  ['A hostile web page talking to your local server', 'An origin guard refuses cross-origin requests and unknown Host names, which stops DNS rebinding. Tokens travel only in headers, and the chat socket opens with a single-use ticket.'],
  ['A public MCP endpoint without a key', '/mcp refuses every request until a key is configured. Keys have scopes, and the gateway sets the scope itself.'],
  ['Tampered or replayed updates', 'Releases and channel pointers are minisign-signed. The updater verifies hashes, rejects unsafe archives and lower sequence numbers, and rolls back on a failed health check. The build side holds no credential for any instance.'],
  ['The agent replacing its own binary', 'Self-update tools are off by default. When on, installing needs an owner approval bound to the exact tree and binary hash.'],
  ['The first stranger to message your bot', 'Chat relays no longer adopt the first sender as owner. You pair explicitly.'],
  ['Cross-person disclosure in shared chats', 'Notes and tasks carry labels, and a shared channel sees only what every verified participant may see. Unknown identities get public content only.'],
  ['Coding agents being clicked through', 'HQ never answers a trust dialog for you, and driving a session has mechanical limits that do not depend on the model deciding to stop.'],
];

const gaps = [
  ['The model itself.', 'A refusal is a mitigation, not a boundary. The boundaries are the sandbox, the environment allowlist and the governance rules. A prompt injection that gets past those is in scope for a report. A model that merely behaves badly is not.'],
  ['The bash text checks.', 'They catch honest mistakes and cheap tricks. Variables, string building, two-step commands and interpreter code can still get through, and the docs list the shapes. Without a working sandbox, you are relying on them plus the environment allowlist.'],
  ['The sandbox itself.', 'HOME stays writable, so shell rc files can be changed and will run later outside the sandbox. The sandbox shares the host network unless you set network to false, and that cuts off gh and git from bash. On macOS, a bash child can still see the daemon\'s environment with ps.'],
  ['Coding agents HQ starts.', 'A harness session is a separate program with its own shell. The host starts each agent from a clean environment and runs it in a process sandbox, but whatever you hand an agent (profile env values, wrapper scripts) is readable by a prompt-injected session. Keep secrets out of profile env.'],
  ['The handoff key.', 'It is equivalent to code execution on every host you paired. Bound it with agent_host.handoff_cwd_allow, and give it only to callers you would give a shell.'],
  ['An attacker who is already you.', 'Anyone who controls the host user, the vault directory or the config file is out of scope. On loopback with no token set, any process on the machine can call the API without an Origin header, so set a token on shared machines.'],
  ['A stolen signing key, or a stale pointer.', 'Both are listed as not mitigated by the updater. A compromised service user can also fake a healthy /health answer to defeat the automatic rollback. Locally built self-update binaries are not signed.'],
  ['Content already in the prompt.', 'Vault text the context engine injects, and earlier turns in a thread, are not tracked as taint. Only tool results in the current session are.'],
  ['Independent review.', 'HQ has not had an outside security audit. It is version 0.9.x. Treat it that way.'],
];

const keyId = '51FDC63C4F4E8BD2';
const keyLine = 'RWTSi05PPMb9UVVnGilhLWT7h/mjQ1VjfAEXszxJB/Er8UEsCXFc3o1/'; // gitleaks:allow
const dl = `V=<version>   # for example 0.9.1, without the leading v\nB=${REPO}/releases/download/v$V\ncurl -fsSLO "$B/manifest.json"\ncurl -fsSLO "$B/manifest.json.minisig"\ncurl -fsSLO "$B/hq-$V-linux-x86_64.tar.gz"\ncurl -fsSLO "${REPO}/raw/main/release/minisign.pub"`;
const verify = 'minisign -Vm manifest.json -p minisign.pub';
const hashCheck = `jq -r '.artifacts[] | "\\(.sha256)  \\(.name)"' manifest.json | sha256sum -c --ignore-missing`;
const dry = 'hq update --apply --dry-run';
---

<Layout
  title="Agent HQ security model and signed releases"
  description="What Agent HQ protects against, what it does not, how to verify a signed release, and how to report a vulnerability."
  path="/security/"
>
  <section class="sec sec-hero" aria-labelledby="sec-h">
    <span class="orb orb-b o-tl" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    <span class="orb orb-i o-tr" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    <span class="orb orb-g o-c slow" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    <div class="container stack">
      <div class="hero-grid">
        <div class="stack">
          <p class="eyebrow">Security model</p>
          <h1 id="sec-h" class="display">
            <span class="hl"><span>What holds.</span></span>
            <span class="hl"><span>What does not.</span></span>
            <span class="hl"><span class="accent">How to check.</span></span>
          </h1>
          <div class="rule rule-in" aria-hidden="true"></div>
          <p class="lede fade-in hero-lede">
            HQ runs tool-using agents that can execute shell commands. That is the risk, so this page says what
            holds, what does not, and how to check the parts that ship to your server.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="vault-art">
          <img
            src="/media/art/vault.jpg"
            alt="Flat isometric illustration: a vault cube with a round barred door inside a stepped wall, small cube figures passing parcels through one checked gate."
            width="1600"
            height="995"
            decoding="async"
          />
          <span class="vscan" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <ul class="vchips list-plain" aria-hidden="true">
            <li class="vchip glass-heavy"><span class="dot dot-green"></span>Sandbox required</li>
            <li class="vchip glass-heavy"><span class="dot dot-blue"></span>Env allowlist and taint</li>
            <li class="vchip glass-heavy"><span class="dot dot-sky"></span>Signed releases</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
      <nav aria-label="On this page">
        <ul class="toc">
          <li><a href="#shapes">Deployment shapes</a></li>
          <li><a href="#protects">What it protects against</a></li>
          <li><a href="#gaps">What it does not</a></li>
          <li><a href="#verify">Verify a release</a></li>
          <li><a href="#report">Report a problem</a></li>
        </ul>
      </nav>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sec sec-tight" id="shapes" aria-labelledby="shapes-h">
    <span class="orb orb-i o-c slow" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    <div class="container stack">
      <h2 id="shapes-h" class="reveal">Supported deployment shapes</h2>
      <div class="shapes">
        <article class="gcard reveal">
          <div class="mini" aria-hidden="true"><span class="loop"><code>127.0.0.1</code></span><span class="orbit"><i></i></span></div>
          <h3>Local, single user</h3>
          <p class="body">The default. The web server binds to <code>127.0.0.1</code>. The machine and its user are trusted. Set <code>web_auth_token</code> on a shared machine.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="gcard reveal reveal-2">
          <div class="mini" aria-hidden="true"><span class="bubble"><span class="pill glass-light">Phone</span><span class="pill pill-green">HQ</span></span><span class="tpacket"></span></div>
          <h3>Private network</h3>
          <p class="body">HQ stays on loopback behind <code>tailscale serve</code> or a reverse proxy. List the served origins in <code>web_allowed_origins</code>.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="gcard reveal reveal-3">
          <div class="mini" aria-hidden="true">
            <span class="gate"></span>
            <span class="lane ln1"><span class="ok">/mcp + key</span></span>
            <span class="lane ln2"><span class="ok ok-2">/health</span></span>
            <span class="lane ln3"><span class="no glass-light">/ws and /api</span></span>
          </div>
          <h3>Public /mcp</h3>
          <p class="body">Only through a proxy that exposes <code>/mcp</code> and <code>/health</code> and nothing else, with <code>AGENTHQ_API_KEY</code> set. <code>/ws</code> and <code>/api</code> must never be public.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sec sec-tight" id="protects" aria-labelledby="protects-h">
    <span class="orb orb-b o-tr" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    <span class="orb orb-g o-bl slow" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    <div class="container stack">
      <div class="head">
        <h2 id="protects-h" class="reveal">What it protects against</h2>
        <p class="lede reveal">
          Each line is a control that exists in the code and is described in the repository docs. None of them is a
          promise that nothing can go wrong.
        </p>
      </div>
      <ul class="prot list-plain">
        {
          protects.map(([threat, control], i) => (
            <li class={`gcard prot-card reveal${i % 2 ? ' reveal-2' : ''}`}>
              <svg class="shield" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M12 3l8 3v6c0 4.5-3.2 8-8 9-4.8-1-8-4.5-8-9V6z"></path><path class="chk" d="M9 12l2 2 4-4"></path></svg>
              <h3 class="h3-sm">{threat}</h3>
              <p class="body">{control}</p>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sec sec-tight" id="gaps" aria-labelledby="gaps-h">
    <span class="orb orb-i o-c" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    <div class="container stack">
      <div class="head">
        <div class="tags reveal"><span class="tag tag-dashed">Known gaps</span></div>
        <h2 id="gaps-h" class="reveal">What it does not protect against</h2>
        <p class="lede reveal">Plain list of limits, taken from the project's own security notes.</p>
      </div>
      <ul class="gaps list-plain">
        {
          gaps.map(([head, body], i) => (
            <li class={`gap glass reveal${i % 3 === 1 ? ' reveal-2' : i % 3 === 2 ? ' reveal-3' : ''}`}>
              <span class="num glass-light gap-num">{String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span>
              <h3 class="h3-sm">{head}</h3>
              <p class="body">{body}</p>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sec sec-tight" id="verify" aria-labelledby="verify-h">
    <span class="orb orb-g o-tr" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    <span class="orb orb-b o-bl slow" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    <div class="container stack">
      <div class="head">
        <h2 id="verify-h" class="reveal">Verifying a signed release</h2>
        <div class="prose reveal">
          <p>
            The updater does this for you, in process, on every update. You can repeat it by hand. The trust chain is
            the minisign signature on <code>manifest.json</code>, then the SHA-256 of each artifact in that signed
            manifest. <code>SHA256SUMS</code> in the release is unsigned and for humans, so do not rely on it alone.
          </p>
          <p>
            Get the official public key from the repository file <a href={links.officialKey}><code>release/minisign.pub</code></a>,
            not from a page that could be altered, and compare. Its key id is <code>{keyId}</code> and its key line begins
            <code>{keyLine.slice(0, 12)}</code>. Install the <a href={links.minisign}>minisign</a> tool and <code>jq</code> first.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="panel glass-heavy shine zoom-in">
        <p class="label chain-title">Trust chain</p>
        <ol class="chain list-plain" aria-label="The public key verifies the manifest signature, the signed manifest lists a hash per artifact, and each artifact must match its hash.">
          <li class="link-node glass-light"><span class="tick" aria-hidden="true">&#10003;</span><code>minisign.pub</code><span class="label">From the repo</span></li>
          <li class="link-node glass-light"><span class="tick" aria-hidden="true">&#10003;</span><code>manifest.json.minisig</code><span class="label">Good signature</span></li>
          <li class="link-node glass-light"><span class="tick" aria-hidden="true">&#10003;</span><code>manifest.json</code><span class="label">SHA-256 per artifact</span></li>
          <li class="link-node glass-light"><span class="tick" aria-hidden="true">&#10003;</span><code>hq-&lt;V&gt;-linux-x86_64.tar.gz</code><span class="label">Hash matches</span></li>
        </ol>
      </div>
      <ol class="steps vsteps">
        <li class="gcard reveal"><p>Download the manifest, its signature, the binary archive and the key.</p><CodeBlock id="ver-dl" label="Download" code={dl} /></li>
        <li class="gcard reveal reveal-2"><p>Verify the manifest signature. It must report a good signature.</p><CodeBlock id="ver-sig" label="Signature" code={verify} /></li>
        <li class="gcard reveal"><p>Check each downloaded artifact against the hash in the signed manifest.</p><CodeBlock id="ver-hash" label="Hashes" code={hashCheck} /></li>
        <li class="gcard reveal reveal-2"><p>On an instance, <code>--dry-run</code> repeats every check, including the channel pointer, and changes nothing.</p><CodeBlock id="ver-dry" label="Dry run" code={dry} /></li>
      </ol>
      <p class="body reveal note">
        Channel pointers (<code>channel-stable.json</code> and <code>channel-main.json</code>) have their own
        <code>.minisig</code>. Only prehashed signatures are accepted, which is the default of <code>minisign -S</code>.
        Format and trust model: <a href={links.updateSystem}>docs/UPDATE_SYSTEM.md</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sec" id="report" aria-labelledby="report-h">
    <span class="orb orb-b o-c" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    <span class="orb orb-g o-br slow" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    <div class="container report-grid">
      <div class="gcard gcard-indigo shine reveal report">
        <p class="eyebrow">Privately, never in a public issue</p>
        <h2 id="report-h" class="h2-sm">Reporting a vulnerability</h2>
        <p>
          Report privately, not in a public issue. Use <a href={links.reportVulnerability}>GitHub's private vulnerability
          reporting</a> on the repository. If that is unavailable, open a public issue that says only that you have a
          security report and asks for a private channel, with no details.
        </p>
        <p>
          Include what you found, how to reproduce it, the affected version and the impact you expect. Expect an
          acknowledgement within 7 days, and please allow 90 days or until a fix ships before disclosing. Do not include
          real credentials or other people's vault contents. Only the latest release and the latest commit on
          <code>main</code> are supported.
        </p>
        <p>The full policy, including what is in and out of scope, is in <a href={links.securityPolicy}>SECURITY.md</a>.</p>
        <div class="actions"><a class="btn btn-primary" href={links.reportVulnerability}>Report privately</a></div>
      </div>
      <div class="stack-sm">
        <h3 class="reveal">Read the details</h3>
        <ul class="doc-links list-plain">
          <li><a class="glass reveal" href={links.sec.webAuth}>Web and MCP authentication</a></li>
          <li><a class="glass reveal" href={links.sec.bashSandbox}>Bash isolation</a></li>
          <li><a class="glass reveal" href={links.sec.promptInjection}>Prompt-injection containment</a></li>
          <li><a class="glass reveal" href={links.sec.webFetch}>Outbound fetches</a></li>
          <li><a class="glass reveal" href={links.sec.selfUpdate}>Self-update tools</a></li>
          <li><a class="glass reveal" href={links.sec.agentEnv}>What a coding agent can see of your environment</a></li>
          <li><a class="glass reveal" href={links.sec.identity}>Identity-scoped disclosure</a></li>
          <li><a class="glass reveal" href={links.sec.releaseChecklist}>Release checklist</a></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .hero-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) auto;
    gap: 48px;
    align-items: center;
  }
  .hero-lede {
    max-width: 560px;
  }
  .vault-art {
    position: relative;
    width: 520px;
    height: 400px;
  }
  .vault-art img {
    position: absolute;
    right: -40px;
    top: 0;
    width: auto;
    max-width: none;
    height: 100%;
    mix-blend-mode: lighten;
    pointer-events: none;
  }
  .vscan {
    position: absolute;
    right: 30px;
    top: 60px;
    width: 300px;
    height: 2px;
    background: var(--brand-green);
    box-shadow: 0 0 18px var(--brand-green);
    opacity: 0.8;
  }
  .vchips {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    pointer-events: none;
  }
  .vchip {
    position: absolute;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    padding: 8px 16px;
    border-radius: var(--radius-pill);
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 700;
    z-index: 2;
  }
  .vchip:nth-child(1) {
    left: 8px;
    top: 64px;
  }
  .vchip:nth-child(2) {
    left: 40px;
    top: 176px;
    animation-delay: 0.8s;
  }
  .vchip:nth-child(3) {
    left: 0;
    top: 288px;
    animation-delay: 1.6s;
  }

  .shapes {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: var(--space-4);
  }
  .mini {
    position: relative;
    height: 150px;
    border-radius: 14px;
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.03);
    border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.06);
    overflow: hidden;
    margin-bottom: 6px;
  }
  .loop {
    position: absolute;
    left: 50%;
    top: 50%;
    width: 110px;
    height: 110px;
    margin: -55px 0 0 -55px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    border: 2px dashed var(--hairline);
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
  }
  .loop code {
    font-size: 12px;
  }
  .orbit {
    position: absolute;
    left: 50%;
    top: 50%;
    width: 0;
    height: 0;
  }
  .orbit i {
    position: absolute;
    left: -5px;
    top: -60px;
    width: 10px;
    height: 10px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--brand-green);
  }
  .bubble {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 18px 24px;
    border-radius: var(--radius-pill);
    border: 2px solid rgba(0, 173, 238, 0.4);
    background: rgba(0, 173, 238, 0.06);
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-around;
  }
  .tpacket {
    position: absolute;
    top: 50%;
    left: 24%;
    width: 12px;
    height: 12px;
    margin-top: -6px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--brand-blue);
    box-shadow: 0 0 12px var(--brand-blue);
  }
  .gate {
    position: absolute;
    left: 50%;
    top: 14px;
    bottom: 14px;
    width: 10px;
    margin-left: -5px;
    border-radius: var(--radius-pill);
    background: var(--brand-indigo);
  }
  .lane {
    position: absolute;
    left: 12px;
    right: 12px;
    height: 24px;
  }
  .ln1 {
    top: 22px;
  }
  .ln2 {
    top: 62px;
  }
  .ln3 {
    top: 102px;
  }
  .lane span {
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    padding: 2px 8px;
    border-radius: var(--radius-pill);
  }
  .ok {
    background: var(--brand-green);
    color: #000000;
  }
  .ok-2 {
    animation-delay: 1.3s;
  }
  .no {
    color: var(--ink);
    animation-delay: 0.6s;
  }

  .prot {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 14px;
    margin: 0;
  }
  .prot-card {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 40px minmax(0, 1fr);
    column-gap: 16px;
    row-gap: 8px;
    align-items: start;
  }
  .prot-card .shield {
    grid-row: span 2;
  }
  .shield {
    width: 40px;
    height: 40px;
    fill: none;
    stroke: var(--brand-green);
    stroke-width: 1.8;
    stroke-linecap: round;
    stroke-linejoin: round;
  }
  .chk {
    stroke-dasharray: 12;
    stroke-dashoffset: 0;
  }
  .h3-sm {
    font-size: 18px;
    line-height: 24px;
  }

  .tag-dashed {
    border-style: dashed;
    color: var(--brand-sky);
  }
  .gaps {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 14px;
  }
  .gap {
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    padding: 22px;
    border: 1px dashed rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.24);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 10px;
  }
  .gap-num {
    color: var(--brand-sky);
  }

  .chain-title {
    margin-bottom: 14px;
  }
  .chain {
    display: flex;
    align-items: stretch;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 10px;
  }
  .link-node {
    flex: 1 1 180px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 6px;
    align-items: center;
    border-radius: 16px;
    padding: 14px 16px;
    text-align: center;
  }
  .link-node code {
    background: none;
    border: 0;
    padding: 0;
    font-size: 13px;
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }
  .tick {
    width: 24px;
    height: 24px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    font-size: 12px;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: #000000;
    background: var(--brand-green);
    border: 2px solid var(--brand-green);
  }
  .link-node:nth-child(2),
  .link-node:nth-child(2) .tick {
    animation-delay: 2s;
  }
  .link-node:nth-child(3),
  .link-node:nth-child(3) .tick {
    animation-delay: 4s;
  }
  .link-node:nth-child(4),
  .link-node:nth-child(4) .tick {
    animation-delay: 6s;
  }
  .vsteps {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: var(--space-4);
  }
  .vsteps > li {
    padding-left: var(--space-5);
    padding-top: 64px;
  }
  .vsteps > li::before {
    left: var(--space-5);
    top: var(--space-5);
  }
  .note {
    max-width: 860px;
  }

  .report-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 24px;
    align-items: start;
  }
  .report {
    padding: 40px;
    gap: 16px;
  }
  .doc-links {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 8px;
  }
  .doc-links a {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    min-height: 52px;
    height: 100%;
    padding: 8px 14px;
    border-radius: 12px;
    color: var(--ink);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-size: 15px;
  }
  .doc-links a:hover {
    border-color: rgba(34, 255, 55, 0.45);
  }

  @media (max-width: 960px) {
    .hero-grid {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    }
    .vault-art {
      width: 100%;
      max-width: 600px;
      justify-self: center;
    }
    .shapes,
    .prot,
    .vsteps,
    .report-grid {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
